data.content:
Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — markup with `@typeparam TItem`, a loop over the internal list using `@key`, and Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — `partial class` code-behind that:
- Copies `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the parent's list).
- Swaps elements on button click, then invokes `OnOrderChanged` with the new order as `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`.

Usage matches your example — just name the template `ItemTemplate`:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = new() { /* ... */ };

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
    {
        tasks = newOrder.ToList();
    }
}
```
